table_structure.prompt:
You are given the phrases of one PDF page region, each with an id, its text and its box (a phrase is words of one line that sit close together, e.g. "€ 1.500" or "12 punten"). A table has ≥2 columns whose phrases line up vertically on several consecutive lines; a bulleted or numbered list, headings and running text are not tables. Find the table(s) among them and return their STRUCTURE only: JSON {"tables": [{"rows": [[["<phrase id>", ...], ...], ...]}]}. Each row is a list of cells left to right; rows go top to bottom; each cell is a list of phrase ids in reading order, or {"words": [...], "colspan": n, "rowspan": n} for a spanning cell; an empty cell is []. Assign whole phrases. Only if one phrase clearly spans two columns, use its word ids (listed under Words) instead. Use every phrase inside a table exactly once and never write any text yourself: only ids from the lists. Phrases outside tables are not part of the answer.

Phrases:
{chunks_json}

Words:
{words_json}
